        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0,
          "end": 2.49,
          "en": "[Maximilian Schwarzmuller] At this point in the course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.49,
          "end": 4.47,
          "en": "you of course already learned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.47,
          "end": 8.25,
          "en": "how you can extract user input from forms,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.25,
          "end": 11.28,
          "en": "for example, with two-way binding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.28,
          "end": 14.76,
          "en": "or with help of template variables",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.76,
          "end": 18.96,
          "en": "and with help of the ngSubmit event",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.96,
          "end": 22.26,
          "en": "to which you can listen, which is provided by Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.26,
          "end": 25.5,
          "en": "We did already use these features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.5,
          "end": 28.35,
          "en": "in earlier course sections.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.35,
          "end": 30.66,
          "en": "But in this course section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.66,
          "end": 35.01,
          "en": "we'll actually dive a bit deeper into managing forms",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.01,
          "end": 36.54,
          "en": "because it turns out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.54,
          "end": 40.68,
          "en": "that besides the approaches we took thus far,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.68,
          "end": 44.88,
          "en": "Angular actually offers two main ways",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.88,
          "end": 48.51,
          "en": "of handling forms in Angular applications.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.51,
          "end": 50.07,
          "en": "If you want to call it like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 50.07,
          "end": 53.88,
          "en": "it has two main approaches you might want to use,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.88,
          "end": 58.88,
          "en": "which allow you to do more than just extract entered values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 59.49,
          "end": 62.91,
          "en": "And that would be template-driven forms",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 62.91,
          "end": 65.04,
          "en": "and reactive forms.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 65.04,
          "end": 68.37,
          "en": "So managing forms in Angular applications",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 68.37,
          "end": 72.03,
          "en": "in a template-driven or reactive way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 72.03,
          "end": 73.5,
          "en": "And we'll take a closer look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.5,
          "end": 76.53,
          "en": "at these two different approaches in this section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 76.53,
          "end": 79.14,
          "en": "and you will of course learn how to use them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.14,
          "end": 80.94,
          "en": "and how to manage your forms",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 80.94,
          "end": 83.46000000000001,
          "en": "with these approaches.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 83.46000000000001,
          "end": 87,
          "en": "We'll explore how you can manage form inputs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87,
          "end": 90.57,
          "en": "how you can extract user input values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 90.57,
          "end": 93.81,
          "en": "and how you can also validate those inputs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 93.81,
          "end": 96.96000000000001,
          "en": "and make sure that only valid values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 96.96000000000001,
          "end": 99.12299999999999,
          "en": "are accepted and used.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 100.28999999999999,
          "end": 102.66,
          "en": "And therefore, for this section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 102.66,
          "end": 105.21000000000001,
          "en": "I prepared another starting project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 105.21000000000001,
          "end": 107.46000000000001,
          "en": "which you find attached as always.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 107.46000000000001,
          "end": 108.78,
          "en": "And after downloading it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 108.78,
          "end": 111.57,
          "en": "you should of course run npm install once",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 111.57,
          "end": 114.15,
          "en": "to install all dependencies.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 114.15,
          "end": 117.63,
          "en": "And then npm starts to start that development server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 117.63,
          "end": 119.03999999999999,
          "en": "And if you do that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 119.03999999999999,
          "end": 123.18,
          "en": "you should then see a page like this on the screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 123.18,
          "end": 126.06,
          "en": "and it's now this basic login form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 126.06,
          "end": 127.92,
          "en": "with which we'll get started,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 127.92,
          "end": 130.71,
          "en": "before we'll then also build a more complex form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 130.71,
          "end": 132.213,
          "en": "later in this section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 133.14,
          "end": 135.24,
          "en": "But before we do any of that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 135.24,
          "end": 138.54,
          "en": "I'll actually first give you a brief overview",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 138.54,
          "end": 141.9,
          "en": "of the template-driven and reactive forms approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 141.9,
